<title>BELGIUM: EU experts discuss genetically-modified maize. [CORRECTED 14:06 GMT]</title>
<headline>EU experts discuss genetically-modified maize. [CORRECTED 14:06 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's cereals management committee on Thursday held an exchange of views on the issue of genetically-modified maize but deferred further discussion, an EU official said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;The Commission put the item on the agenda in order to canvass the views of member states,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>Three scientific committees are currently studying the question and are expected to report before Christmas.</p>
<p>Discussion on national aid to the EU food aid scheme was deferred.</p>
<p>Consideration of tenders for manioc from Thailand and third countries as well as for sweet potatoes and manioc starch was also deferred. (Corrects by deleting all references to a decision on a tender for 100,000 tonnes of maize from northern Greece being deferred. The tender was approved and will go ahead).</p>
</text>
